quran[25]{c,v,t}:
  76,26,"And prostrate before Him, in some part of the night, and glorify Him by night at length."
  76,27,"Indeed, these (disbelievers) love this transitory life and (neglectfully) put a tough day behind them."
  76,28,"We created them and strengthened their physical structure. And when We wish, We can easily replace them with others like them."
  76,29,"This (Qur’an) is indeed a Reminder. So whoever wishes, let him take the (right) path towards his Lord."
  76,30,"But you cannot wish (to do so) unless Allah wills (it). Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
  76,31,"He admits whomever He pleases into His mercy. But as for the wrongdoers, He has prepared a painful punishment for them."
  77,1,"By those (pleasant winds) sent forth successively,"
  77,2,"by those (storming winds) blowing violently,"
  77,3,"by those (spreading winds) scattering (rain clouds) widely,"
  77,4,"by those (discerning winds) splitting (the clouds) apart forcefully,"
  77,5,"by the inspirers of the Reminder,"
  77,6,"to end excuses or give warnings,"
  77,7,"indeed, what you are promised will certainly occur."
  77,8,"So when the stars are made to lose their light,"
  77,9,"and when the heavens are split apart,"
  77,10,"and when the mountains are blown away (like dust),"
  77,11,"and when the time is set for the messengers (to witness),"
  77,12,for what Day has all this been set (to occur)?
  77,13,For the Day of Judgement!
  77,14,What will make you realise what the Day of Judgement is?
  77,15,Woe to the deniers on that Day!
  77,16,"Did We not destroy the earlier generations (of deniers),"
  77,17,and then We will cause the later ones to follow them (in destruction)?
  77,18,This is how We deal with the guilty.
  77,19,Woe to the deniers on that Day!
